=circuit.positive_input&relation=prerequisites","prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=22326593cd4ee37735df71d5e7612efdc02bf148d61a9361dc2d26629a464dbf&view=arguments&node=circuit.positive_input&assumptions=true"},"neighborhood_href":"/api/v1/neighborhood?manifest=22326593cd4ee37735df71d5e7612efdc02bf148d61a9361dc2d26629a464dbf&ref=sha256%3Af22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92%2Fnodes%2Fcircuit.positive_input","record":{"assumption_ids":[],"boundary":"This is the alternative branch’s explicitly imported external input family. It does not use the zero-temperature full-support theorem. The ordered-Gaussian normalization and mean-zero diagonal correction are fixed before applying the external result. The Lopatto theorem is source-reported here, not independently proved.","citation_ids":["circuit-r2-26-cite-positive-input","lopatto2026_interval_support"],"evidence_ids":[],"id":"circuit.positive_input","kind":"assumption","label":"Independent finite-temperature input family","locator":"07-positive-temperature.tex:3–129; eq:positive-parisi-pde, eq:positive-parisi-value, eq:positive-parisi-diffusion","source_id":"circuit-r2-26-source-positive","statement":"For every fixed β₀>1, import the finite-temperature Parisi formula and a minimizing Parisi measure μ_{β₀} with support [0,q_{β₀}], q_{β₀}<1, from the stated interval-support result. With γ=β₀μ([0,t]), terminal β₀^(−1)log(2cosh(β₀x)), m=Φ_x and a=Φ_xx, import the bounded-strip regularity, diffusion and contact identity E[m(t,X_t)²]=t for 0≤t≤q_{β₀}, and dm=a dW.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/circuit.positive_input","relations":[{"derived":true,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/circuit.positive_mesh","id":"field:135692c19bb0a838ae58919010018b2d7bf1340026bfc0a45fb5fb20cbd78d75","kind":"assumption_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c0682921